<title>CANADA: Canadian lumber data delayed, export fees likely.</title>
<headline>Canadian lumber data delayed, export fees likely.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>An end-of-quarter rush is delaying publication of statistics of Canadian softwood lumber exports to the United States, but some exporters will probably have to pay export fees, an official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;They're still sorting through the backlog,&quot; said Charles Larabie, spokesman at the Department of Foreign Affairs and International Trade.</p>
<p>The complication was that as exporters realized that the quarterly limit of 28.75 percent of an annual duty-free export quota to the United States of 14.7 billion board feet was nearly breached, some cancelled their export permits.</p>
</text>
